### 9. Impact and Significance

The proposed system helps businesses understand customer opinions without manually reading a large number of reviews. By automatically classifying customer feedback into positive, negative, and neutral categories, organizations can identify customer satisfaction levels, discover common complaints, and understand the strengths and weaknesses of their products.

The project demonstrates the practical application of **Natural Language Processing, machine learning, and artificial intelligence** to a real-world business problem. It can also help students understand the complete NLP pipeline, from text preprocessing and feature extraction to model training and evaluation.

---

### 10. Deliverables

The project will deliver:

* An AI-powered Product Review Sentiment Analysis application.
* A cleaned and processed product review dataset.
* An NLP-based text preprocessing pipeline.
* A trained sentiment classification model.
* Classification of reviews into positive, negative, and neutral categories.
* A simple user interface for entering and analyzing product reviews.
* Visualizations showing sentiment distribution.
* Source code and project documentation.
* Project report including methodology, implementation, results, and evaluation.

---

# Problem Statement

With the rapid growth of e-commerce platforms, customers generate thousands of product reviews that contain valuable information about their experiences and opinions. However, manually analyzing a large number of reviews is time-consuming and makes it difficult for businesses to quickly identify customer satisfaction and common complaints.

The proposed project aims to develop an **AI-Based Sentiment Analysis System for Product Reviews using Natural Language Processing**. The system will automatically analyze the textual content of product reviews and classify them into **positive, negative, or neutral** sentiment categories. NLP techniques will be used to preprocess the review text, extract meaningful features, and identify sentiment patterns. Machine learning or transformer-based models will then be used to perform the classification.

The performance of the proposed system will be evaluated using metrics such as **accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and confusion matrix**. The system will help businesses efficiently analyze customer feedback, understand customer satisfaction, and identify areas for product or service improvement. The project will demonstrate the practical application of NLP and artificial intelligence in solving a real-world text classification problem.
